<title>CANADA: Canada Grain Commission details wheat test results.</title>
<headline>Canada Grain Commission details wheat test results.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Grain Commission on Thursday detailed preliminary milling and baking test results for white No1 Canada Prairie Spring Wheat. PRELIMINARY DATA ON No1 Canada Prairie Spring Wheat - White</p>
<p>Quality Parameters		 1996	     1995</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>  Test weight (kg/hl)	    82.7	     81.5</p>
<p>  Weight per 1,000 kernels, g  38.3	     37.9</p>
<p>  Protein Content (pct)	  10.9	     10.6</p>
<p>  Dry Matter Protein (pct)     12.6	     12.3</p>
<p>  Ash Content (pct)		 1.38	     1.45</p>
<p>  Alpha-amylase Activity unit/g 6.0		6.0</p>
<p>  Falling Number		  365		385</p>
<p>  Flour Yield (pct)		76.9	     76.8</p>
<p>  PSI (pct)			  60		 63</p>
<p>FLOUR</p>
<p>  Protein Content (pct)	  10.1		9.9</p>
<p>  Wet Gluten Content (pct)     28.2	     30.4</p>
<p>  Ash Content (pct)		 0.50	     0.49</p>
<p>  Grade Colour, K-J units	-1.7	     -0.8</p>
<p>  AGTRON Colour (pct)	    70		 66</p>
<p>  Starch damage, Megazyme units 5.3	     n/a</p>
<p>  Starch damage, AACC units     8.0		8.1</p>
<p>  Alpha-amylase Activity unit/g 1.0		2.0</p>
<p>  Amylograph Peak Viscosity, BU 900		580</p>
<p>  Maltose Value, g/100 g	  1.7		1.8</p>
<p>  Zeleny Sedimentation, mL     38		 39</p>
<p>FARINOGRAM</p>
<p>  Absorption (pct)		 60.6	     60.6</p>
<p>  Development Time, mins.	 2.50	     2.50</p>
<p>  Mixing Tolerance Index, BU   80		 90</p>
<p>  Stability, mins.		  3.00	     3.50</p>
<p>N.B.: unless otherwise noted, data based on 13.5 pct wheat moisture and 14.0 pct flour moisture.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
